          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भान — bhān — \"awareness; consciousness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खेळताना मुलांना वेळेचं भान राहिलं नाही. kheḷtānā mulānnā veḷecaṁ bhān rāhilaṁ nāhī. While playing, the children lost track of time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "X चं भान (bhān) ठेवणे, to keep X in mind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भान (bhān) is a tatsama, taken from Sanskrit bhāna, \"appearance\" (CDIAL 9451): what appears to the mind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
